# Root-level environment variables.
#
# Per-app env lives in each app's own .env / .env.example: the Discord bot's
# in apps/discord-bot/.env.example; the web app's dev server needs none. A local script's credentials are committed as
# 1Password references instead (apps/discord-bot/.env.example, tools/r2.op.env),
# resolved by `op run --env-file=<file> -- <command>`; never put a secret in
# either. None of the VITE_-prefixed variables below is a secret — anything
# VITE_-prefixed is inlined into the browser bundle, so never put one there
# that is.

# --- apps/web ---
# Commit SHA, sent as the release with each browser error report. CI and the
# deploy pass it in.
VITE_COMMIT_REF=
